{"assets":["/editorial-assets/d15a9f0b37ff956e6bb8a590c6bea0c331f4648b65c65bb077025c67dd783da2.png","/editorial-assets/6cb4fcc26674340813458a970c53fd67f03faab3007c458d62fe3d89a19a351c.png","/editorial-assets/40a5b98db6be113e29896e691b46d1fcc5c8d6589eb3e867eabaf9ada646d125.png","/editorial-assets/44ec28d44f41d0aabb950dd8b714e6ad3309eaa9c97e38b977bd08a8b705bc1a.png","/editorial-assets/fc2a0b19866c3099cf0fd0aed6173fb633663393f096cfbfcd801910c73d2994.png","/editorial-assets/64317211b5be06442027daeddb87d3081e15dcdf37c70ae2d9216b065c505d95.png"],"contestId":"825","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"825A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/825/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"825A - Binary Protocol"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's decode the number digit by digit starting from the leftmost. When you meet '1' in the string, increase the value of the current digit. For '0' print current digit and proceed to the next one. Don't forget to print the last digit when the string is over."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"825B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/825/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"825B - Five-In-a-Row"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This one is a pure implementation task. Just check every possible line of length 5. If the current one contains 4 crosses and 1 empty cell then the answer is 'YES'."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"825C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/825/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"825C - Multi-judge Solving"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Obviously sorting the tasks by difficulty will always produce the most optimal order of solving. In that case ability to solve some task "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" will mean ability to solve any task from 1 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now let's maintain the upper limit of difficulty of problem Makes is able to solve. Right after solving some problem "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" it will be 2·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Initially it's just 2·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Transition from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 will then look like this. If the upper limit it greater or equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" then we solve this problem and update the upper limit. Otherwise we will need some problems from other judges. As our goal is to maximize the upper limit, the most optimal task to solve is the hardest possible. So you should solve task with the difficulty of upper limit and update the limit itself. Keep doing it until upper limit becomes grater or equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You will require no more then "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/d15a9f0b37ff956e6bb8a590c6bea0c331f4648b65c65bb077025c67dd783da2.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" tasks from the other judges. By algorithm it's easy to see that by solving task with difficulty "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we update upper limit with the value 2·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". This function produces such a estimate."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/6cb4fcc26674340813458a970c53fd67f03faab3007c458d62fe3d89a19a351c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"825D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/825/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"825D - Suitable Replacement"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Notice that the order of letters doesn't matter at all, suitability depends only on amount of each letter."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the possibility that string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" will occur in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" at least "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" times after replacing all '?' signs and after some swaps. If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is true then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is also true. That leads to binary search over the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cntT"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the amount of letters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cntS"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the amount of letters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"qcnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the number of '?' signs. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is true if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/40a5b98db6be113e29896e691b46d1fcc5c8d6589eb3e867eabaf9ada646d125.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". If some letter appears in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" less times than needed then replace some '?' signs with it. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Answer can be restored greedily by replacing '?' signs with the letters needed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/44ec28d44f41d0aabb950dd8b714e6ad3309eaa9c97e38b977bd08a8b705bc1a.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"AL"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the size of the alphabet."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"825E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/825/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"825E - Minimal Labels"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This problem is usually called \"Topological labelling\". Though it's pretty common problem, we decided that it might be educational to some of participants."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's set labels in descending order starting from label "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to label 1. Look at first step. Vertex with label "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" should have out-degree equal to zero. Among all such vertices we should put the label on the one that has the largest index. Ok, but why will this produce the lexicographically smallest labelling?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can prove this by contradiction. Let this vertex be labeled "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Change it to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and renumerate vertices with label "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1, ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to labels "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1. Labelling will come lexicographically smaller than it was, this leads to contradiction."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So the algorithm comes as following. On step "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"... 1) we find vertices with out-degree equal to zero, select the one with the largest index, set its label to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and remove this vertex (and all edges connected to it) from the graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Current minimal out-degree can be maintained with set, for example."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/fc2a0b19866c3099cf0fd0aed6173fb633663393f096cfbfcd801910c73d2994.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"825F"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/825/problem/F"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"825F - String Compression"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] be the answer for the prefix of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" consisting of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" first characters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How can we update "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")? Suppose that we try to represent the substring from index "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to index "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 (0-indexed) by writing it as some other string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" times. Then this string has to be the smallest period of the substring, and "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/64317211b5be06442027daeddb87d3081e15dcdf37c70ae2d9216b065c505d95.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the length of the smallest period."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The smallest period of some string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be calculated as follows: compute prefix-function for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and if |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| is divisible by |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"last"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"last"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the last value of prefix-function), then the length of the smallest period is |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"last"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" (if not, then the length of the smallest period is |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This allows us to write a solution with complexity "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). To improve it to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"), we can use the fact that when we compute prefix-function for some string, we compute it for every prefix of this string. So to obtain all values of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"last"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" we need in our solution, we only need to compute prefix-functions for every suffix of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"825G"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/825/problem/G"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"825G - Tree Queries"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After the first query make the vertex that we painted black the root of the tree and for each other vertex calculate the minimum index on the path to the root. This can be done by simple DFS."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then suppose we are painting some vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" black. In can easily proved that for every vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and every vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" that is on a path form "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the root there exists a path from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to some black vertex coming through "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". So we have to store the minimum index among all vertices "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" belongs to the path from the root to some black vertex (it is a global value, let's call it "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"globalMin"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), and the answer to every query of type 2 is just the minimum of the value we calculated in DFS and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"globalMin"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". To update "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"globalMin"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" quickly after painting vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" black, we ascend from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the root until we arrive to some node that was visited during previous queries (and we stop there because this node and all nodes on the path from it to the root were used to update "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"globalMin"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in previous queries)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This solution works in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") time."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/53334"}